+````markdown name=ops/helm/production_k8s_manifests.md
+```text
+Guidance & examples: minimal Kubernetes manifests to deploy and harden production services.
+
+This document contains short example manifests and guidance. For full production, convert to Helm charts.
+
+1) Namespace & secrets
+---
+apiVersion: v1
+kind: Namespace
+metadata:
+  name: aegis
+
+Create secrets via:
+kubectl create secret generic aegis-mlflow-secrets --from-literal=MLFLOW_DB_PASS=... -n aegis
+
+2) MLflow deployment (example)
+---
+apiVersion: apps/v1
+kind: Deployment
+metadata:
+  name: mlflow
+  namespace: aegis
+spec:
+  replicas: 2
+  selector: { matchLabels: { app: mlflow }}
+  template:
+    metadata: { labels: { app: mlflow } }
+    spec:
+      serviceAccountName: aegis-mlflow
+      containers:
+        - name: mlflow
+          image: ghcr.io/aegis/mlflow:latest
+          env:
+            - name: MLFLOW_TRACKING_URI
+              value: "http://mlflow:5000"
+            - name: MLFLOW_BACKEND_STORE_URI
+              value: "postgresql+psycopg2://mlflow:$(MLFLOW_DB_PASS)@mlflow-db:5432/mlflow_db"
+          resources:
+            requests: { cpu: "500m", memory: "1Gi" }
+            limits: { cpu: "1", memory: "2Gi" }
+          volumeMounts:
+            - name: mlflow-artifacts
+              mountPath: /mlflow_artifacts
+      volumes:
+        - name: mlflow-artifacts
+          persistentVolumeClaim:
+            claimName: mlflow-artifacts-pvc
+
+3) Milvus (example helm recommended)
+ - Use the milvus helm chart with production_values_milvus.yml provided earlier.
+
+4) Network policy & RBAC
+ - Apply network policies to default-deny and only allow control-plane/service-to-service as in ops/hardening/namespace_networkpolicies.yaml
+ - Create service accounts for each service and bind RBAC rules minimally (ops/helm/production_rbac.yaml)
+
+5) Backups & restore
+ - Use CronJobs in ops/backup/prod_backup_cronjobs.yaml for nightly backups.
+
+Operational notes:
+ - Use PodSecurity admission and PodSecurityPolicy equivalents on legacy clusters.
+ - Secrets: use Vault integration via CSI driver; do NOT store long-lived secrets in k8s secrets.
+ - Use nodeSelectors and tolerations to schedule GPU/TPU/Neuron workloads to specialized node pools.
+
